cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "setmm_choice: axiom-dependency analysis and proof repair for Metamath"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vincent
    family-names: Gonzalez
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3640-014X"
    email: vincegonzalez@me.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/vince-gonzalez/setmm_choice"
abstract: >-
  The Metamath arm of gonzalgo. Measures which theorems in a Metamath database
  depend on a given axiom, ranks them by how many other theorems would stop
  depending on it if each were repaired (dominator analysis over the proof DAG
  rooted at the axiom), and constructs and verifies replacement proofs.
  Includes a census of the library's own `$j usage ... avoids` guard directives
  and the general-domination defect class analysis. Seven repairs built against
  set.mm, six submitted, one merged (PR #5442, freeing 36 theorems including
  Bayes' theorem from the axiom of choice).
keywords:
  - metamath
  - set.mm
  - formal verification
  - axiom of choice
  - proof assistant
  - dependency analysis
  - dominator analysis
license: MIT
